    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Modified Parkland: 3–4 mL/kg/%TBSA Hartmann's in the first 24 h, half in the first 8 h from time of burn; titrate to urine output 0.5 mL/kg/h (adults), 1 mL/kg/h (children) — avoid fluid creep.",
